### 1. Summary of Test Pass Cases

All test cases passed successfully. Below are the corresponding project code implementations along with their pseudocode representations.

#### 1.1 `test_create_experiment`
**Key Functionality:** This test verifies that creating an experiment initializes all relevant fields and saves them correctly to a file. 

**Pseudocode:**
```
CLASS Experiment:
    FUNCTION __init__(title: str, objectives: str, materials: str, procedures: str):
        SET self.title = title
        SET self.objectives = objectives
        SET self.materials = materials
        SET self.procedures = procedures
        SET self.status = "Not Started"

    FUNCTION get_details() -> str:
        RETURN formatted string containing title, objectives, materials, procedures, and status

    FUNCTION record_observation(observation: str) -> None:
        OPEN 'observations/{self.title}_observations.txt' in append mode AS obs_file:
            WRITE observation to obs_file

FUNCTION save_to_file(experiment_data: dict, filename: str) -> None:
    OPEN filename in write mode AS file:
        FOR each key-value pair IN experiment_data:
            WRITE key and value to file in format 'key|value'

FUNCTION load_from_file(filename: str) -> dict:
    INITIALIZE experiment_data as empty dictionary
    IF filename exists:
        OPEN filename in read mode AS file:
            FOR each line IN file:
                SPLIT line by '|' INTO key, value
                SET experiment_data[key] = value
    RETURN experiment_data
```

#### 1.2 `test_delete_experiment`
**Key Functionality:** This test ensures that an experiment can be deleted, verifying the removal of the corresponding file.

**Pseudocode:**
```
CLASS Main:
    FUNCTION delete_experiment(title: str) -> None:
        SET self.experiments = [exp FOR exp IN self.experiments IF exp.title != title]
        REMOVE file 'experiments/{title}.txt' from the filesystem
```

#### 1.3 `test_edit_experiment`
**Key Functionality:** This test checks whether the details of an existing experiment can be edited and that the changes are saved correctly.

**Pseudocode:**
```
CLASS Main:
    FUNCTION edit_experiment(title: str, objectives: str, materials: str, procedures: str) -> None:
        FOR experiment IN self.experiments:
            IF experiment.title == title:
                SET experiment.objectives = objectives
                SET experiment.materials = materials
                SET experiment.procedures = procedures
                CALL self.save_experiment(experiment)

    FUNCTION save_experiment(experiment: Experiment) -> None:
        SET experiment_data as dictionary with title, objectives, materials, procedures
        CALL save_to_file(experiment_data, 'experiments/{experiment.title}.txt')
```

